UI: {
	ButtonTip: Vanity Studio
	SwitchToAchievements: Show the achievement advisor here
	SwitchToStudio: Show the Vanity Studio button here
	SlotHead: Head
	SlotBody: Body
	SlotLegs: Legs
	SlotFront: Front
	SlotBack: Back
	NewName: New {0}
	NamePlaceholder: Design name
	TipSlot:
		'''
		What this is worn as.
		Click for next, right-click for previous
		'''
	HideVanilla: Replace vanilla look
	TipHideVanilla:
		'''
		Hide the vanilla sprite in this slot while the design is worn.
		Your armor keeps all of its stats, only the look changes
		'''
	TipClose: Close (Esc). Everything is saved automatically
	TipEquip: Wear this design
	TipUnequip: Take this design off
	TipExport: Export a vanilla-layout sprite sheet (.png) and a shareable .vsd file
	TipImport: Import a .png sprite / sheet into a new layer, or open a .vsd design
	TipFromEquipped: Copy the sprite of the armor or accessory you're showing in this slot into a new layer, so you can repaint it
	TipSave: Save now (Ctrl+S)
	TipLibrary: All your designs
	TipUndo: Undo (Ctrl+Z)
	TipRedo: Redo (Ctrl+Y)
	Saved: Saved
	Equipped: Wearing {0}
	Exported: Exported {0}
	ExportedChat: "[Vanity Studio] Exported to {0}"
	ExportFailed: Export failed, see client.log
	ImportTitle: Import into Vanity Studio
	ImportFailed: Couldn't read that file
	Imported: Imported {0}
	ImportedEquipped: Copied {0} into a new layer
	NothingEquipped: Nothing visible in the {0} slot to copy
	TooManyLayers: Too many layers
	ToolPencil: Pencil
	ToolEraser: Eraser
	ToolFill: Fill
	ToolPicker: Color picker
	ToolLine: Line
	ToolRect: Rectangle (hold Shift to fill)
	ToolMove: Move layer
	TipBrush: Brush size ([ and ])
	TipMirror: Mirror horizontally (M)
	TipGrid: Pixel grid
	TipReference: Show the character under the canvas ({0}%, scroll to change)
	PoseBase: All poses
	TipPoseBase: Draw once for every pose. The walk bob is added for you
	PoseStand: Stand
	PoseJump: Jump
	PoseUse: Swing {0}
	PoseWalk: Walk {0}
	GroupUse: Swing
	GroupWalk: Walk
	TipPoseOverride: Has its own drawing. Right-click to go back to the base drawing
	TipPoseInherit: Uses the base drawing. Draw here to give this pose its own version
	UsingBase: showing base
	TipLayerAdd: New layer
	TipLayerDuplicate: Duplicate layer
	TipLayerDelete: Delete layer
	TipLayerUp: Move layer up
	TipLayerDown: Move layer down
	TipLayerMerge: Merge into the layer below
	LayerName: Layer {0}
	TipFrameAdd: New empty frame
	TipFrameDuplicate: Duplicate frame
	TipFrameDelete: Delete frame
	TipFrameLeft: Move frame left
	TipFrameRight: Move frame right
	TipPlay: Play / pause (Enter)
	TipOnion: Onion skin (O)
	TipDuration: Frame duration. Scroll or click, Shift for bigger steps
	All: All
	TipDurationAll: Use this duration for every frame
	Opacity: Opacity
	TipVisible: Show / hide layer
	TipRename: Double-click to rename
	FrameN: frame {0}
	FramesN: "{0} frames"
	TipCelClear: Right-click to clear (only the selected pose)
	TipTurn: Turn around
	PvAuto: Auto
	PvIdle: Idle
	PvWalk: Walk
	PvJump: Jump
	PvFly: Fly
	PvUse: Swing
	PvPose: Pose
	TipSwapColors: Swap colors (X)
	Clear: Clear
	TipTransparent: Transparent: paint with it to erase
	RightClickHint: right click paints with the back color
	CharacterColors: Your character
	Recent: Recent
	LibraryTitle: Designs ({0})
	LibraryEmpty: Nothing here yet
	OpenFolder: Open folder
	ImportFile: Import...
	NewFor: New:
	TipOpen: Open in the editor
	TipDuplicate: Duplicate
	TipDelete: Delete
	TipDeleteConfirm: Click again to delete for good
	TipHelp: How does this work? (replays the walkthrough)
	TipLayerFlip: Flip what's on screen horizontally. Shift: whole layer
	TipLayerOutline: Add a 1px outline in the main color around the drawing. Shift: whole layer
	HintPencil: LMB: main color, RMB: back color, Alt: pick color.
	HintEraser: Click and drag to erase.
	HintFill: Click to fill an area. Shift+click: replace that color everywhere.
	HintPicker: LMB / RMB: take the color for the main / back slot.
	HintLine: Drag to draw a straight line.
	HintRect: Drag for a rectangle. Hold Shift to fill it.
	HintMove: Drag to shift the whole drawing.
	HintNav: Wheel: zoom · Middle mouse / Space+drag: pan · F: fit
	TipPreview: Live preview (x{0}). Scroll to zoom
	Show: Show:
	FilterAll: All
	TipNewFor: Start a new {0} design
	Layers: Layers
	TutDontShow: Don't show this again
	TutNext: Next
	TutBack: Back
	TutSkip: Skip
	TutFinish: Let's go!
	TutWelcomeTitle: Welcome to Vanity Studio!
	TutWelcome:
		'''
		Here you can draw your own hats, shirts, trousers, capes and wings, or repaint armor you already own.
		This quick tour shows where everything is. It takes under a minute, and you can skip it now and reopen it later with the ? button.
		'''
	TutSetupTitle: Name, slot and look
	TutSetup:
		'''
		Give the design a name and pick what it is: Head, Body, Legs, Front (scarves, belts) or Back (capes, wings).
		"Replace vanilla look" hides the sprite of whatever you're wearing in that slot, so your design takes its place. Stats never change.
		'''
	TutToolsTitle: Tools
	TutTools:
		'''
		Pencil, eraser, fill, color picker, line, rectangle and move. Under them: brush size, mirror drawing, the pixel grid, and your character shown under the canvas.
		Every tool has a keyboard shortcut, hover a button to see it.
		'''
	TutCanvasTitle: Canvas
	TutCanvas:
		'''
		This is the same 40x56 frame the game uses, so what you draw sits exactly where it will on your character. The faded character underneath is there to help you line things up.
		Left click paints with the main color, right click with the back color. Scroll to zoom, hold the middle mouse button to move around.
		'''
	TutPosesTitle: Poses
	TutPoses:
		'''
		"All poses" is where you'll draw most of the time: it's used for every pose, and the little walking bounce is added for you.
		If a pose needs its own version (a cape flapping on a walk frame, a sleeve while swinging), pick that pose and draw: a gold dot marks poses with their own drawing. Right-click a pose to undo that.
		'''
	TutTimelineTitle: Layers and frames
	TutTimeline:
		'''
		On the left are your layers: add, duplicate, reorder, merge, hide them and change their opacity. Double-click a name to rename it.
		On the right is the timeline. Add frames to animate the design and set how long each frame lasts. Onion skin shows the neighbouring frames.
		'''
	TutPreviewTitle: Live preview
	TutPreview: Your character wearing the design as you draw. Auto runs through standing, walking, jumping, flying and swinging; or pick a single action. Scroll over it to zoom.
	TutColorsTitle: Colors
	TutColors: The big square is the main color, the one behind it is the back color, click them to swap. Use the sliders, type a hex code, or pick from the palette, your character's own colors and recently used ones.
	TutActionsTitle: Saving, sharing, importing
	TutActions:
		'''
		Undo/redo, all your designs, save, copy the armor you're wearing into a layer to repaint it, import a .png, and export a sprite sheet.
		You don't have to press save: everything is saved automatically and shows up on every character, world and server.
		'''
	TutWearTitle: Wear it
	TutWear:
		'''
		Press this to put the design on. It stays on this character between sessions, and players on the same server see it too, even while you're still drawing.
		Have fun!
		'''
}
